{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.evaporative",
    "description": "Template library: the two shapes the EVAPORATIVE chain adds, from docs/evap-leaks.md §4.2 and §4.3. Both are small, and both are here rather than inline because the arithmetic either side of them looks alike and the difference is load-bearing.\n\n`operating_share_of_activity` is E1, crates/moves-calculators/src/generators/evap_op_mode_distribution.rs:350 -- `least(1, SUM(SHO) / SUM(sourceHours))`, with the zero-denominator guard that `COALESCE(SUM(SHO), 0)`'s other half implies. It is NOT lib/onroad_activity.esm's `share_of_group`, and merging the two would be wrong in both directions: `share_of_group` has no cap, and a cap on a normalisation would silently change the travel fraction of docs/mixed-onroad.md S3.\n\n`soak_share` is E2, :443 stage 2 -- `soakActivityFraction * (1 - fractionOfOperating)`. One product, two parameters, and a name. The name is the point. E3's operating-mode-300 fraction is `greatest(0, 1 - SUM(soak shares))`, a RESIDUAL over a different set, and the two subtractions are easy to confuse: on the process-evap-leaks fixture `fractionOfOperating` is exactly 1, so `opModeFraction[300] = fractionOfOperating` and `opModeFraction[300] = 1 - SUM(...)` agree to the last bit and only one of them is right (docs/evap-leaks.md §2.3 measures the difference on a probe as 6.8e-08). Naming the soak half makes the residual half conspicuous by NOT having a template.\n\nDeliberately absent: a `clamp01`. There are two clamps in this stage, `least(1, .)` at E1 and `greatest(0, .)` at E3, with different bodies and different constants, and in both cases the VALUE the clamp takes is the load-bearing fact. A shared template would hide which clamp is which -- the same reasoning lib/onroad_activity.esm records for declining to factor the two onroad clamps. Also absent: the `/ noOfRealDays` of L9. It appears once, and it is the third thing in this port that carries a 7-day week and combines it differently from the other two (lib/conversion.esm's `temporal_scale` and lib/onroad_activity.esm's `weeks_per_month`); three templates for three combinations, none merged.\n\nAs with every library here, an `enums` block is file-local and does not cross a template import (esm-spec §9.3, finding F3), so identifier values arrive as parameters the call site binds to `enum` ops.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "onroad", "evaporative", "template-library"]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "operating_share_of_activity": {
      "params": ["sho_total", "source_hours_total"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["source_hours_total", 0.0] },
          { "op": "min", "args": [1.0, { "op": "/", "args": ["sho_total", "source_hours_total"] }] },
          0.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "soak_share": {
      "params": ["soak_activity_fraction", "operating_share"],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          "soak_activity_fraction",
          { "op": "-", "args": [1.0, "operating_share"] }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
